<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσανά-κλητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard to call back</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.74e
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.18.8
			</span></i> (but simply, <i>hard to summon, call together</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				24
			</span></i>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hard to restore</i>, of hysterics, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.29
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.74
			</span></i>; or to good spirits, <i><span class="en">
				Max.Tyr.
				33.6
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔχειν</span> to be <i>hard to restore</i>
			to one's senses, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				16
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
